---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { DATA_STORYTELLING } from '../../../../courses/data-storytelling/syllabus';
---
<CourseHome course={DATA_STORYTELLING}>
  <p class="cs-meta"><strong>Try it now:</strong> <a href="/learn/courses/data-storytelling/choosing-a-chart/">chart chooser</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/data-storytelling/declutter/">clean up a chart step by step</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/data-storytelling/action-titles/">write a chart title and get feedback</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/data-storytelling/glossary/">glossary</a></p>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>What you will be able to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Say your point in one sentence</strong> and shape a short story around it: situation, complication, resolution.</li>
      <li><strong>Pick the right chart</strong> for any business question, and spot charts that mislead.</li>
      <li><strong>Turn a default chart into a clear one</strong>: remove clutter, use grey plus one colour, label directly and write a title that states the point.</li>
      <li><strong>Design KPI cards and dashboards</strong> that pass the five-second test, with fair comparisons like like-for-like growth.</li>
      <li><strong>Present to managers</strong>: answer first, handle tough questions, and follow up so a decision gets made.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every lesson has charts you can change, before and after examples, writing practice with instant feedback, and a 3-question quiz. It uses the same made-up shop as <a href="/learn/courses/power-bi/">Power BI and DAX</a>, so you can build the dashboard there and tell its story here.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
